+/// The GOT idiom `ldr r1,[pc,#imm]; ldr r1,[pc,r1]` composes its address into
+/// a temporary and dereferences it. The address is never held in a register,
+/// so it is a cell read, not an address-taken relation or a claim about the
+/// value loaded out of that cell.
+#[test]
+fn a_composed_temporary_load_references_the_cell_without_an_address_taken_claim() {
