diff --git a/docs/spec/00-overview.md b/docs/spec/00-overview.md
index ce499c4f..9d927aa5 100644
--- a/docs/spec/00-overview.md
+++ b/docs/spec/00-overview.md
@@ -3431,3 +3431,98 @@ Reserving it creates no analysis varnode and changes no physical mapping or
 emitted C. Ghidra receives temporary storage for the logical local, rather than
 a persistable ordinary stack-variable location; ordinary symbol storage and
 register-plus-stack parameter JOINs keep their existing encoding.
+
+## Experimental read-only atomic facts
+
+The same opt-in capture also exports an independent version-1 `atomic_switches`
+facet. One membership scan supplies recovered BRANCHIND identities. Native
+jump-table rows retain their original index, optional label/status, original
+target address and native row-to-out-edge mapping. Indexes are never treated as
+case values or mapped by comparing optimized block start addresses. Missing
+tables/labels/mappings, the reserved no-label marker and partial tables remain
+explicit. A native model default out-edge is separate from any machine
+out-of-range guard destination. Selector values and consumed-bit masks do not establish runtime
+feasibility or machine semantic equivalence; the native signed-label flag is a
+render hint, not a general signedness proof.
+
+Construction admits 12,000 switches, 100,000 rows and row/edge mappings, and a
+2 MiB shared selector/type/address-space text budget. Mapping is indexed once
+instead of scanning every edge for every case. New switch rows cannot displace
+otherwise fitting existing graph/call facts: the bounded document writer retries
+without this facet first, retains explicit capacity errors, and can still keep
+the independent rows if other facets overflow. Ordinary non-opt-in analysis and
+executable bytes are unchanged.
+
+The opt-in `decompile --json --atomic-facts` surface captures the same live
+function after C rendering (`decompiler/crates/kuna-decomp/src/substrate/atomic_facts.rs`).
+It does not change the analysis phases or C output. The default path does not
+collect these records. This experiment requires embedded processor specs and
+selects those assets explicitly; a caller-provided `--sleighpath` is rejected.
+
+The export retains ordered basic-block predecessors and successors, slotmap
+value identities, operation sequence identities, operand indexes, outputs and
+phi input-to-predecessor-edge bindings. IDs belong to this captured function
+model; instruction addresses are origins, not SSA value identities. Native
+recovered graph completeness does not establish runtime successor coverage,
+memory alias dependencies or machine-semantic equivalence. Indirect-branch
+operations and definitions outside block membership remain explicit. Capacity
+failures make this facet unavailable with a reason and preserve the C record;
+they do not emit a clipped graph labeled complete.
+
+`--atomic-output-bytes N` sets the encoded document budget (default 8 MiB).
+Atomic JSON uses the ordinary record producer and the shared compact ASCII-safe
+writer. That writer checks each encoded write before growing its bounded output
+buffer, including control/surrogate escaping and the final newline. A document
+that cannot fit omits unavailable recovered facets with named errors and
+retains C, locations and ordinary metadata. If that base record also cannot fit,
+the command reports failure instead of truncating it or analyzing the target
+again. This flag requires `--atomic-facts --json`; ordinary output is unchanged.
+
+Graph schema version 3 and an independent `atomic_calls` version-1 facet are
+captured from the same live function after C rendering. The call facet scans
+all native block members without allocating a copy of every block's operations;
+it has its own call/input/value/text limits. Full-graph capacity failure leaves
+calls and their boundary values available. Shared value extraction owns the
+native value identities, flags, widths and definitions; boundary values do not
+claim a complete function value/definition graph.
+
+`FuncCallSpecs` supplies recovered targets, names, prototype flags and passing
+storage. Target input zero remains an SSA value (often an fspec annotation),
+never a callee code address. CALLIND targets can remain unknown. Storage uses
+matching-arity finalized locations or locked prototype storage; shifted inputs
+and placeholders stay unknown. Input slots are not source parameter ordinals.
+
+The encoded writer attempts bounded facet alternatives without cloning their
+contents. A raw schema-3 graph that fits keeps its existing format. Before
+dropping useful facts, an oversized graph can use a schema-4 envelope with
+`encoding: "gzip-base64"`, the exact `raw_bytes` and canonical padded `data`.
+Its decompressed JSON is the unchanged logical schema-3 graph. Raw encoding
+stops at 32 MiB; compressed output, base64 expansion and envelope overhead are
+bounded before allocation against the caller's encoded budget. All graphs in a
+document share that encoded budget. Optional compression does not analyze again.
+The independent full-graph row limits are 32,000 operations, 36,000 values,
+100,000 inputs, 4 MiB display/type text, 12,000 blocks and 50,000 CFG edges.
+They bound construction separately from wire size; exceeding them is unavailable,
+not a complete clipped graph. C and independent calls keep their own contracts.
+A full graph omits its redundant operation projection; if encoded
+capacity makes that graph unavailable, the independent projection is restored.
+A fitting graph has priority, then fitting calls, then the projection. Failed
+facets retain named errors. If C itself cannot fit, output fails explicitly
+without reanalysis. Facet errors do not fabricate empty collections or change C.
+
+`atomic_membership.rs` owns one checked scan of recovered block membership and
+call roots. Its optional index is bounded at 65,536 native operation keys; calls
+remain readable beyond that index budget. `atomic_operations.rs` normalizes
+operands, phi bindings, origins, outputs, display and values for both full and
+selected exports. Full-graph operation capacity is checked before materializing
+its rows, after the common scan.
+
+The independent version-1 `atomic_projection` retains all recovered calls as
+roots, then follows backward operand definitions within a 4,096-operation,
+12,288-value, 16,384-input and 2 MiB text budget. Too many roots or unavailable
+membership make this facet unavailable. Omitted defining operations have exact
+IDs and `operation-budget` or `outside-recovered-membership` frontier reasons.
+This does not collect CFG or complete use lists, infer memory aliases, or prove
+runtime reachability. Collection uses the same live function after C rendering;
+no second decompilation is performed. Complete source Evidence keeps the native
+frontier while callers may select a compact summary and individual facts.
